From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:39:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 140/148] docs(gastown): make claim-status and role-prompt
 prose match gc 1.5.0 and the restack (gcp-fooz4)

- approval-fallacy.template.md and the polecat prompt said a claimed step
  bead "is still stored open". That is gc 1.4.x only: gc 1.5.0's
  `gc hook --claim` promotes the claim to in_progress (cmd_hook_claim.go:750
  requires the readback to be in_progress), and a `--claim` update always
  did. The `open,in_progress` filter is unchanged; the reason is now
  version-neutral.
- Both copies also said "a molecule's work bead is never assigned to the
  polecat session", false since 0060: workspace-setup holds it in_progress
  for the session from that step on.
- gastown/README.md "Role prompts point at formulas" forbade restated
  commands, but the restack restored the crash-recovery copies of
  `next-iteration` in the witness, deacon, refinery and boot prompts, which
  upstream also carries and pins (test_witness_wisp_queries_pin_include_infra).
  Its boot exception ("single-pass watchdog with no formula") has been false
  since upstream #261 gave boot mol-boot-patrol. The section is now "Role
  prompts and formula commands": the formula step owns the command, and a
  prompt either points at it or carries a complete copy naming it.
- The matching comments in test_gastown_pack_assets.sh and the drift test's
  docstrings follow.

Prose and test comments only; test_prompt_formula_command_drift.py and
test_gastown_pack_assets.sh stay green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
